# Topology DSL

This Livebook defines and activates two local Agents with one ownership
relationship.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define A Cell Agent

```elixir
defmodule TopologyGuide.Cell do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "topology_guide_cell"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{label: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default("cell")})
  end

  routes do
    route "jido.agent.child.*" do
      action _input, name: "topology_guide_child_lifecycle", context: context do
        {:ok, context.agent_state}
      end
    end
  end
end
```

## Declare A Topology

```elixir
defmodule TopologyGuide.System do
  use Jido.Topology, name: "topology_guide_system"

  agents do
    agent :leader, TopologyGuide.Cell do
      initial_state %{label: "leader"}
    end

    agent :worker, TopologyGuide.Cell do
      initial_state %{label: "worker"}
    end
  end

  relationships do
    owns :leader, :worker do
      on_parent_exit :stop
    end
  end

  startup do
    concurrency 2
    max_agents 10
    task_timeout 5_000
  end
end
```

## Build The Plan

```elixir
topology = TopologyGuide.System.new!(id: "guide-system", input: %{})

%{
  id: topology.id,
  layer_count: length(topology.plan.layers),
  member_count: map_size(topology.plan.agents)
}
```

Construction and planning start no processes.

## Activate The System

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()

{:ok, controller} =
  Jido.Topology.Controller.start_link(
    jido: Jido.default_instance(),
    topology: topology
  )

:ok = Jido.Topology.Controller.await_ready(controller)

leader = Jido.Topology.Controller.whereis_agent(controller, :leader)
worker = Jido.Topology.Controller.whereis_agent(controller, :worker)

%{
  leader: Jido.AgentServer.agent(leader).state,
  worker: Jido.AgentServer.agent(worker).state,
  leader_children: Jido.AgentServer.children(leader)
}
```

## Stop The Example

```elixir
:ok = Supervisor.stop(controller)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

A normal controller shutdown stops its topology Agents.

Continue with [Topology Builders, Codecs, And Composition](topology-builders-codecs-and-composition.md).
